IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa25-names-ch2.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 41 "Business names", Chapter 2 "Disclosure required in
-- case of individual or partnership" and Chapter 3 "Supplementary": ss 1200 to 1208 (lines 16916-16995 of
-- ukpga-2006-46.txt). Layer 1: the law, objectively.
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; it is not the
-- official text and nothing here is "verified against the official text". Quote lines are checked by srcrefs.py.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer; NOTES.md, "Reading a result").
--   JUST TRUE   the text says yes (for a "has complied" function: every requirement that engages is met).
--   JUST FALSE  the text says no in its own words: -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "<quoted words>"
--   NOTHING     the text does not decide: -- NOTHING-kind (<why>), <why> being one of: silent, list not closed,
--               includes, undefined term, points outside the text, limited by its own wording.
--   A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Chapter 2 applies to an individual or a partnership, not to a company (s 1200(1)). Answers other parts give are INPUTS
-- under the names PLAN.md section 4 gives them (s 1121). Every name below begins with the section label it implements.

§ `Part 41: business names`

§§ `Chapter 2: disclosure required in case of individual or partnership`

-- ---- s 1200: Application of this Chapter -----------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 1200 kind of person` IS ONE OF
    `s 1200 an individual`
    `s 1200 a partnership`
    `s 1200 another kind of person`

DECLARE `s 1200 addition` IS ONE OF
    `s 1200 an individual's forename or initial`
    `s 1200 the forenames of individual partners or the initials of those forenames`
    `s 1200 the addition of "s" at the end of a surname shared by two or more individual partners`
    `s 1200 an addition merely indicating that the business is carried on in succession to a former owner of the business`
    `s 1200 any other addition`

-- src:16918 | 1200 Application of this Chapter
-- src:16919 | (1) This Chapter applies to an individual or partnership carrying on business in the United Kingdom under a business name.
-- src:16920 | References in this Chapter to “a person to whom this Chapter applies” are to such an individual or partnership.
@ref s 1200(1) Application of this Chapter (src:16918-16920)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 1200 kind of person`
      `the person carries on business in the United Kingdom under a business name` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1200(1) the person is a person to whom this Chapter applies` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 1200 another kind of person` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "References in this Chapter to “a person to whom this Chapter applies” are to such an individual or partnership" (a defined expression; the scope sentence alone would answer NOTHING: fork F12)
    OTHERWISE
        IF `the person carries on business in the United Kingdom under a business name`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This Chapter applies to an individual or partnership carrying on business in the United Kingdom under a business name"

-- src:16927 | (3) The following are the permitted additions—
-- src:16928 | (a) in the case of an individual, his forename or initial;
-- src:16929 | (b) in the case of a partnership—
-- src:16930 | (i) the forenames of individual partners or the initials of those forenames, or
-- src:16931 | (ii) where two or more individual partners have the same surname, the addition of “s” at the end of that surname;
-- src:16932 | (c) in either case, an addition merely indicating that the business is carried on in succession to a former owner of the business.
@ref s 1200(3) The permitted additions (src:16927-16932)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 1200 kind of person`
      addition IS A `s 1200 addition`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1200(3) the addition is a permitted addition` MEANS
    CONSIDER addition
    WHEN `s 1200 an individual's forename or initial` THEN
        CONSIDER kind
        WHEN `s 1200 an individual` THEN JUST TRUE -- (a)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) in the case of an individual, his forename or initial" (a list the text hands the definition to: the 2026-11-05 ruling)
    WHEN `s 1200 the forenames of individual partners or the initials of those forenames` THEN
        CONSIDER kind
        WHEN `s 1200 a partnership` THEN JUST TRUE -- (b)(i)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) in the case of a partnership— (i) the forenames of individual partners or the initials of those forenames"
    WHEN `s 1200 the addition of "s" at the end of a surname shared by two or more individual partners` THEN
        CONSIDER kind
        WHEN `s 1200 a partnership` THEN JUST TRUE -- (b)(ii)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) in the case of a partnership— ... (ii) where two or more individual partners have the same surname, the addition of “s” at the end of that surname"
    WHEN `s 1200 an addition merely indicating that the business is carried on in succession to a former owner of the business` THEN
        CONSIDER kind
        WHEN `s 1200 another kind of person` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) in either case": either an individual or a partnership
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE -- (c)
    WHEN `s 1200 any other addition` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The following are the permitted additions" (a list the text hands the definition to: the 2026-11-05 ruling)

-- src:16921 | (2) For the purposes of this Chapter a “business name” means a name other than—
-- src:16922 | (a) in the case of an individual, his surname without any addition other than a permitted addition;
-- src:16923 | (b) in the case of a partnership—
-- src:16924 | (i) the surnames of all partners who are individuals, and
-- src:16925 | (ii) the corporate names of all partners who are bodies corporate,
-- src:16926 | without any addition other than a permitted addition.
@ref s 1200(2) "Business name" (src:16921-16926)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 1200 kind of person`
      `the name consists of the individual's surname, or of the surnames of all the partners who are individuals and the corporate names of all the partners who are bodies corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
      additions IS A LIST OF `s 1200 addition`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1200(2) the name is a business name` MEANS
    IF kind EQUALS `s 1200 another kind of person`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(a) in the case of an individual ... (b) in the case of a partnership"
    ELSE IF `the name consists of the individual's surname, or of the surnames of all the partners who are individuals and the corporate names of all the partners who are bodies corporate`
            AND all (GIVEN a YIELD `s 1200(3) the addition is a permitted addition` kind a EQUALS JUST TRUE) additions
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a “business name” means a name other than— (a) in the case of an individual, his surname without any addition other than a permitted addition; (b) in the case of a partnership— (i) the surnames of all partners who are individuals, and (ii) the corporate names of all partners who are bodies corporate, without any addition other than a permitted addition"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- ---- s 1201: Information required to be disclosed -------------------------------------------------------

-- src:16933 | 1201 Information required to be disclosed
-- src:16934 | (1) The “information required by this Chapter” is—
-- src:16935 | (a) in the case of an individual, the individual's name;
-- src:16936 | (b) in the case of a partnership, the name of each member of the partnership;
-- src:16937 | and, in relation to each person so named, an address at which service of any document relating in any way to the business will be effective.
@ref s 1201(1) The information required by this Chapter (src:16933-16937)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 1200 kind of person`
      `the disclosure states the name of the individual, or the name of each member of the partnership` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure states, for each person so named, an address at which service of any document relating in any way to the business will be effective` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1201(1) the disclosure contains the information required by this Chapter` MEANS
    IF kind EQUALS `s 1200 another kind of person`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(a) in the case of an individual ... (b) in the case of a partnership"
    ELSE IF `the disclosure states the name of the individual, or the name of each member of the partnership`
            AND `the disclosure states, for each person so named, an address at which service of any document relating in any way to the business will be effective`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The “information required by this Chapter” is— (a) in the case of an individual, the individual's name; (b) in the case of a partnership, the name of each member of the partnership; and, in relation to each person so named, an address at which service of any document relating in any way to the business will be effective"

-- src:16938 | (2) If the individual or partnership has a place of business in the United Kingdom, the address must be in the United Kingdom.
@ref s 1201(2) The address must be in the United Kingdom if there is a place of business there (src:16938)
GIVEN `the individual or partnership has a place of business in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the address is in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1201(2) the address meets the requirement as to place` MEANS
    IF NOT `the individual or partnership has a place of business in the United Kingdom`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- the requirement does not engage, so nothing is left to fail (fork F5)
    ELSE IF `the address is in the United Kingdom`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the individual or partnership has a place of business in the United Kingdom, the address must be in the United Kingdom" (a bare "must" not met: decided at this site, fork F5)

-- src:16939 | (3) If the individual or partnership does not have a place of business in the United Kingdom, the address must be an address at which service of documents can be effected by physical delivery and the delivery of documents is capable of being recorded by the obtaining of an acknowledgement of delivery.
@ref s 1201(3) The address where there is no place of business in the United Kingdom (src:16939)
GIVEN `the individual or partnership has a place of business in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `service of documents can be effected at the address by physical delivery` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the delivery of documents is capable of being recorded by the obtaining of an acknowledgement of delivery` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1201(3) the address meets the requirement as to delivery` MEANS
    IF `the individual or partnership has a place of business in the United Kingdom`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- the requirement does not engage, so nothing is left to fail (fork F5)
    ELSE IF `service of documents can be effected at the address by physical delivery`
            AND `the delivery of documents is capable of being recorded by the obtaining of an acknowledgement of delivery`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the individual or partnership does not have a place of business in the United Kingdom, the address must be an address at which service of documents can be effected by physical delivery and the delivery of documents is capable of being recorded by the obtaining of an acknowledgement of delivery" (a bare "must" not met: decided at this site, fork F5)

-- ---- s 1202: Disclosure required: business documents etc ----------------------------------------------------
-- Subsections (3) and (4) are a regulation-making power and its procedure (inert, reason 2).

DECLARE `s 1202 kind of document` IS ONE OF
    `s 1202 a business letter`
    `s 1202 a written order for goods or services to be supplied to the business`
    `s 1202 an invoice or receipt issued in the course of the business`
    `s 1202 a written demand for payment of a debt arising in the course of the business`
    `s 1202 another document`

-- src:16941 | 1202 Disclosure required: business documents etc
-- src:16942 | (1) A person to whom this Chapter applies must state the information required by this Chapter, in legible characters, on all—
-- src:16943 | (a) business letters,
-- src:16944 | (b) written orders for goods or services to be supplied to the business,
-- src:16945 | (c) invoices and receipts issued in the course of the business, and
-- src:16946 | (d) written demands for payment of debts arising in the course of the business.
-- src:16947 | This subsection has effect subject to section 1203 (exemption for large partnerships if certain conditions met).
@ref s 1202(1) Disclosure required on business documents (src:16941-16947)
GIVEN `document kind` IS A `s 1202 kind of document`
      `s 1203(1) the exemption applies to the document` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1202(1) the requirement to state the information applies to the document` MEANS
    IF `s 1203(1) the exemption applies to the document` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Section 1202(1) (disclosure required in business documents) does not apply in relation to a document issued by a partnership of more than 20 persons if the following conditions are met" (s 1203(1))
    ELSE CONSIDER `document kind`
         WHEN `s 1202 another document` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "on all— (a) business letters, (b) written orders ..., (c) invoices and receipts ..., and (d) written demands for payment of debts"
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:16941 | 1202 Disclosure required: business documents etc
-- src:16942 | (1) A person to whom this Chapter applies must state the information required by this Chapter, in legible characters, on all—
-- src:16943 | (a) business letters,
-- src:16944 | (b) written orders for goods or services to be supplied to the business,
-- src:16945 | (c) invoices and receipts issued in the course of the business, and
-- src:16946 | (d) written demands for payment of debts arising in the course of the business.
-- src:16947 | This subsection has effect subject to section 1203 (exemption for large partnerships if certain conditions met).
@ref s 1202(1) Disclosure required on business documents (src:16941-16947)
GIVEN `the requirement to state the information applies to the document` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the information required by this Chapter is stated on the document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is stated in legible characters` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1202(1) the person has complied with the requirement to state the information on the document` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the requirement to state the information applies to the document`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE -- the requirement does not apply to the document, so nothing is left to fail (fork F5)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): subsection (1) names four kinds of document and no other
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the information required by this Chapter is stated on the document` AND `it is stated in legible characters`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person to whom this Chapter applies must state the information required by this Chapter, in legible characters, on all— (a) business letters, ..." (a bare "must" not done: decided at this site, fork F5)

-- src:16948 | (2) A person to whom this Chapter applies must secure that the information required by this Chapter is immediately given, by written notice, to any person with whom anything is done or discussed in the course of the business and who asks for that information.
@ref s 1202(2) The information must be immediately given, by written notice, to a person who asks (src:16948)
GIVEN `a person with whom anything is done or discussed in the course of the business has asked for the information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information was immediately given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was given by written notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1202(2) the person has complied with the requirement to give the information on request` MEANS
    IF NOT `a person with whom anything is done or discussed in the course of the business has asked for the information`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- the requirement does not engage, so nothing is left to fail (fork F5)
    ELSE IF `the information was immediately given` AND `it was given by written notice`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must secure that the information required by this Chapter is immediately given, by written notice, to any person with whom anything is done or discussed in the course of the business and who asks for that information" (a bare "must" not done: decided at this site, fork F5)

-- ---- s 1203: Exemption for large partnerships if certain conditions met --------------------------------------

-- src:16953 | (2) The conditions are that—
-- src:16954 | (a) the partnership maintains at its principal place of business a list of the names of all the partners,
-- src:16955 | (b) no partner's name appears in the document, except in the text or as a signatory, and
-- src:16956 | (c) the document states in legible characters the address of the partnership's principal place of business and that the list of the partners' names is open to inspection there.
@ref s 1203(2) The conditions (src:16953-16956)
GIVEN `the partnership maintains at its principal place of business a list of the names of all the partners` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no partner's name appears in the document, except in the text or as a signatory` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document states in legible characters the address of the partnership's principal place of business and that the list of the partners' names is open to inspection there` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1203(2) the conditions for the exemption are met` MEANS
    IF `the partnership maintains at its principal place of business a list of the names of all the partners`
       AND `no partner's name appears in the document, except in the text or as a signatory`
       AND `the document states in legible characters the address of the partnership's principal place of business and that the list of the partners' names is open to inspection there`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The conditions are that— (a) the partnership maintains at its principal place of business a list of the names of all the partners, (b) no partner's name appears in the document, except in the text or as a signatory, and (c) the document states in legible characters the address of the partnership's principal place of business and that the list of the partners' names is open to inspection there"

-- src:16951 | 1203 Exemption for large partnerships if certain conditions met
-- src:16952 | (1) Section 1202(1) (disclosure required in business documents) does not apply in relation to a document issued by a partnership of more than 20 persons if the following conditions are met.
@ref s 1203(1) Exemption for a partnership of more than 20 persons (src:16951-16952)
GIVEN `the number of persons in the partnership` IS A NUMBER
      `s 1203(2) the conditions for the exemption are met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1203(1) the exemption applies to the document` MEANS
    IF `the number of persons in the partnership` AT MOST 20
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a document issued by a partnership of more than 20 persons"
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 1203(2) the conditions for the exemption are met`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the following conditions are met" (an "if" that is not met)
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the conditions are met is not known

-- src:16957 | (3) Where a partnership maintains a list of the partners' names for the purposes of this section, any person may inspect the list during office hours.
@ref s 1203(3) Any person may inspect the list during office hours (src:16957)
GIVEN `the partnership maintains a list of the partners' names for the purposes of s 1203` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the inspection is during office hours` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1203(3) the person may inspect the list` MEANS
    IF NOT `the partnership maintains a list of the partners' names for the purposes of s 1203`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a partnership maintains a list of the partners' names for the purposes of this section" (a "where" that fails: the 2026-11-05 ruling)
    ELSE IF `the inspection is during office hours`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any person may inspect the list during office hours"

-- src:16958 | (4) Where an inspection required by a person in accordance with this section is refused, an offence is committed by any member of the partnership concerned who without reasonable excuse refused the inspection or permitted it to be refused.
@ref s 1203(4) Offence of refusing an inspection (src:16958)
GIVEN `an inspection required by a person in accordance with s 1203 was refused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the member refused the inspection or permitted it to be refused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the member had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1203(4) the member of the partnership commits an offence` MEANS
    IF NOT `an inspection required by a person in accordance with s 1203 was refused`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an inspection required by a person in accordance with this section is refused" (a "where" that fails: the 2026-11-05 ruling)
    ELSE IF NOT `the member refused the inspection or permitted it to be refused`
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an offence is committed by any member of the partnership concerned who without reasonable excuse refused the inspection or permitted it to be refused"
         ELSE IF `the member had a reasonable excuse`
              THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without reasonable excuse"
              ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:16959 | (5) A person guilty of an offence under subsection (4) is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 1203(5) Penalty for an offence under s 1203 (src:16959)
GIVEN guilty IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 1203(5) the penalty for an offence under s 1203` MEANS
    CONSIDER guilty
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        JUST (Penalty WITH `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
                           `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
                           `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1)
                           `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1)
                           `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE)
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is guilty is not known

-- ---- s 1204: Disclosure required: business premises -----------------------------------------------------
-- Subsections (2) and (3) are a regulation-making power and its procedure (inert, reason 2).

-- src:16960 | 1204 Disclosure required: business premises
-- src:16961 | (1) A person to whom this Chapter applies must, in any premises—
-- src:16962 | (a) where the business is carried on, and
-- src:16963 | (b) to which customers of the business or suppliers of goods or services to the business have access,
-- src:16964 | display in a prominent position, so that it may easily be read by such customers or suppliers, a notice containing the information required by this Chapter.
@ref s 1204(1) Disclosure required at business premises (src:16960-16964)
GIVEN `the premises are premises where the business is carried on` IS A BOOLEAN
      `customers of the business or suppliers of goods or services to the business have access to the premises` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1204(1) the requirement to display the notice applies to the premises` MEANS
    IF NOT `the premises are premises where the business is carried on`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in any premises— (a) where the business is carried on" (a "where" that fails: the 2026-11-05 ruling)
    ELSE IF `customers of the business or suppliers of goods or services to the business have access to the premises`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) to which customers of the business or suppliers of goods or services to the business have access" (a condition of the same "in any premises" clause as (a); this function asks the provision's own question, whether the requirement applies: fork F24)

-- src:16960 | 1204 Disclosure required: business premises
-- src:16961 | (1) A person to whom this Chapter applies must, in any premises—
-- src:16962 | (a) where the business is carried on, and
-- src:16963 | (b) to which customers of the business or suppliers of goods or services to the business have access,
-- src:16964 | display in a prominent position, so that it may easily be read by such customers or suppliers, a notice containing the information required by this Chapter.
@ref s 1204(1) Disclosure required at business premises (src:16960-16964)
