      `a notice containing the information required by this Chapter is displayed in a prominent position, so that it may easily be read by such customers or suppliers` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1204(1) the person has complied with the requirement to display the notice` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the requirement to display the notice applies to the premises`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE -- the requirement does not apply to the premises, so nothing is left to fail (fork F5)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the requirement applies to the premises is not known (the caller's input)
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `a notice containing the information required by this Chapter is displayed in a prominent position, so that it may easily be read by such customers or suppliers`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must ... display in a prominent position, so that it may easily be read by such customers or suppliers, a notice containing the information required by this Chapter" (a bare "must" not done: decided at this site, fork F5)

-- ---- s 1205: Criminal consequences of failure to make required disclosure ---------------------------------

-- src:16969 | (1) A person who without reasonable excuse fails to comply with the requirements of—
-- src:16970 | section 1202 (disclosure required: business documents etc), or
-- src:16971 | section 1204 (disclosure required: business premises),
-- src:16972 | commits an offence.
@ref s 1205(1) Offence of failing without reasonable excuse to comply with s 1202 or s 1204 (src:16969-16972)
GIVEN `s 1202(1) the person has complied with the requirement to state the information on the document` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1202(2) the person has complied with the requirement to give the information on request` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1204(1) the person has complied with the requirement to display the notice` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person has a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1205(1) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    IF `s 1202(1) the person has complied with the requirement to state the information on the document` EQUALS JUST FALSE
       OR `s 1202(2) the person has complied with the requirement to give the information on request` EQUALS JUST FALSE
       OR `s 1204(1) the person has complied with the requirement to display the notice` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN IF `the person has a reasonable excuse`
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who without reasonable excuse fails to comply with the requirements of section 1202 ... or section 1204"
         ELSE JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `s 1202(1) the person has complied with the requirement to state the information on the document` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            AND `s 1202(2) the person has complied with the requirement to give the information on request` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            AND `s 1204(1) the person has complied with the requirement to display the notice` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person who without reasonable excuse fails to comply with the requirements of section 1202 (disclosure required: business documents etc), or section 1204 (disclosure required: business premises), commits an offence" (the offence is defined by the failure: marginal reading (a))
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the requirements were met is not known

-- src:16973 | (2) Where an offence under this section is committed by a body corporate, an offence is also committed by every officer of the body who is in default.
@ref s 1205(2) Offence: every officer of the body corporate who is in default (src:16973)
GIVEN `the body corporate commits an offence under this section` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1205(2) an officer of the body corporate commits an offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the body corporate commits an offence under this section`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an offence under this section is committed by a body corporate, an offence is also committed by every officer of the body who is in default" (a "where" that fails: the 2026-11-05 ruling)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the body corporate commits the offence is not known
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        CONSIDER `s 1121 the officer is in default`
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an offence is also committed by every officer of the body who is in default"
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the officer is in default is the answer of s 1121
-- src:16974 | (3) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 1205(3) Penalty for an offence under s 1205 (src:16974)
GIVEN guilty IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 1205(3) the penalty for an offence under s 1205` MEANS
    CONSIDER guilty
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        JUST (Penalty WITH `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
                           `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
                           `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1)
                           `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1)
                           `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE)
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is guilty is not known

-- src:16975 | (4) References in this section to the requirements of section 1202 or 1204 include the requirements of regulations under that section.
@ref s 1205(4) The requirements of s 1202 or s 1204 include the requirements of regulations (src:16975)
GIVEN `it is a requirement of regulations made under s 1202 or s 1204` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1205(4) the requirement is a requirement of s 1202 or s 1204` MEANS
    IF `it is a requirement of regulations made under s 1202 or s 1204`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "References in this section to the requirements of section 1202 or 1204 include the requirements of regulations under that section"

-- ---- s 1206: Civil consequences of failure to make required disclosure --------------------------------------

-- src:16976 | 1206 Civil consequences of failure to make required disclosure
-- src:16977 | (1) This section applies to any legal proceedings brought by a person to whom this Chapter applies to enforce a right arising out of a contract made in the course of a business in respect of which he was, at the time the contract was made, in breach of section 1202(1) or (2) (disclosure in business documents etc) or section 1204(1) (disclosure at business premises).
@ref s 1206(1) Proceedings to which s 1206 applies (src:16976-16977)
GIVEN `the proceedings are brought by a person to whom Chapter 2 applies to enforce a right arising out of a contract made in the course of a business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at the time the contract was made he was in breach of s 1202(1) or (2) or s 1204(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1206(1) this section applies to the proceedings` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are brought by a person to whom Chapter 2 applies to enforce a right arising out of a contract made in the course of a business`
       AND `at the time the contract was made he was in breach of s 1202(1) or (2) or s 1204(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies to any legal proceedings brought by a person to whom this Chapter applies to enforce a right arising out of a contract made in the course of a business in respect of which he was, at the time the contract was made, in breach of section 1202(1) or (2) ... or section 1204(1)" (a scope limit with no "only": the 2026-11-05 ruling)

-- src:16978 | (2) The proceedings shall be dismissed if the defendant (in Scotland, the defender) to the proceedings shows—
-- src:16979 | (a) that he has a claim against the claimant (pursuer) arising out of the contract that he has been unable to pursue by reason of the latter's breach of the requirements of this Chapter, or
-- src:16980 | (b) that he has suffered some financial loss in connection with the contract by reason of the claimant's (pursuer's) breach of those requirements,
-- src:16981 | unless the court before which the proceedings are brought is satisfied that it is just and equitable to permit the proceedings to continue.
@ref s 1206(2) The proceedings shall be dismissed (src:16978-16981)
GIVEN `s 1206(1) this section applies to the proceedings` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the defendant shows that he has a claim against the claimant arising out of the contract that he has been unable to pursue by reason of the claimant's breach of the requirements of this Chapter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the defendant shows that he has suffered some financial loss in connection with the contract by reason of the claimant's breach of those requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that it is just and equitable to permit the proceedings to continue` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1206(2) the proceedings shall be dismissed` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 1206(1) this section applies to the proceedings`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies to any legal proceedings brought by a person to whom this Chapter applies"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies to ..."
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF NOT (`the defendant shows that he has a claim against the claimant arising out of the contract that he has been unable to pursue by reason of the claimant's breach of the requirements of this Chapter`
                OR `the defendant shows that he has suffered some financial loss in connection with the contract by reason of the claimant's breach of those requirements`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The proceedings shall be dismissed if the defendant (in Scotland, the defender) to the proceedings shows— (a) ... or (b) ..." (an "if" that is not met: marginal reading (a))
        ELSE IF `the court is satisfied that it is just and equitable to permit the proceedings to continue`
             THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the court before which the proceedings are brought is satisfied that it is just and equitable to permit the proceedings to continue" (an "unless" once met: fork F6)
             ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:16982 | (3) References in this section to the requirements of this Chapter include the requirements of regulations under this Chapter.
@ref s 1206(3) The requirements of this Chapter include the requirements of regulations (src:16982)
GIVEN `it is a requirement of regulations made under this Chapter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1206(3) the requirement is a requirement of this Chapter` MEANS
    IF `it is a requirement of regulations made under this Chapter`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "References in this section to the requirements of this Chapter include the requirements of regulations under this Chapter"

-- src:16983 | (4) This section does not affect the right of any person to enforce such rights as he may have against another person in any proceedings brought by that person.
@ref s 1206(4) No effect on the right to enforce rights against another person (src:16983)
GIVEN `the proceedings are brought by a person to enforce rights he may have against another person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1206(4) the section affects the right to enforce rights against another person` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are brought by a person to enforce rights he may have against another person`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not affect the right of any person to enforce such rights as he may have against another person in any proceedings brought by that person"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the flat negative reaches only the enforcement of rights against another person in proceedings brought by that person

-- ---- The duties of ss 1202(1), 1202(2) and 1204(1) as regulative rules ---------------------------------------
-- The text names the person to whom the Chapter applies as the party and gives no time limit (s 1202(2) says
-- "immediately"), so the rules carry no WITHIN; the consequence is the offence of s 1205 (a breach "without reasonable
-- excuse"). They are run with #TRACE in coa25-tests-names-ch2.l4.

DECLARE `s 1202 party` IS ONE OF
    `s 1202 the person to whom Chapter 2 applies`

DECLARE `s 1202 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 1202 state the information required by Chapter 2, in legible characters, on the document`
    `s 1202 give the information required by Chapter 2, immediately and by written notice, to a person who asks`
    `s 1204 display a notice containing the information required by Chapter 2 in a prominent position in the premises`

-- src:16941 | 1202 Disclosure required: business documents etc
-- src:16942 | (1) A person to whom this Chapter applies must state the information required by this Chapter, in legible characters, on all—
-- src:16943 | (a) business letters,
-- src:16944 | (b) written orders for goods or services to be supplied to the business,
-- src:16945 | (c) invoices and receipts issued in the course of the business, and
-- src:16946 | (d) written demands for payment of debts arising in the course of the business.
-- src:16947 | This subsection has effect subject to section 1203 (exemption for large partnerships if certain conditions met).
@ref s 1202(1) Disclosure required on business documents (src:16941-16947)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 1202 party` `s 1202 act`
`s 1202(1) the person must state the information on the document` MEANS
    PARTY `s 1202 the person to whom Chapter 2 applies`
    MUST `s 1202 state the information required by Chapter 2, in legible characters, on the document`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 1202 the person to whom Chapter 2 applies` BECAUSE "s 1202(1): the information required by Chapter 2 was not stated, in legible characters, on the document"

-- src:16948 | (2) A person to whom this Chapter applies must secure that the information required by this Chapter is immediately given, by written notice, to any person with whom anything is done or discussed in the course of the business and who asks for that information.
@ref s 1202(2) The information must be immediately given, by written notice, to a person who asks (src:16948)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 1202 party` `s 1202 act`
`s 1202(2) the person must give the information to a person who asks` MEANS
    PARTY `s 1202 the person to whom Chapter 2 applies`
    MUST `s 1202 give the information required by Chapter 2, immediately and by written notice, to a person who asks`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 1202 the person to whom Chapter 2 applies` BECAUSE "s 1202(2): the information was not immediately given, by written notice, to a person who asked for it"

-- src:16960 | 1204 Disclosure required: business premises
-- src:16961 | (1) A person to whom this Chapter applies must, in any premises—
-- src:16962 | (a) where the business is carried on, and
-- src:16963 | (b) to which customers of the business or suppliers of goods or services to the business have access,
-- src:16964 | display in a prominent position, so that it may easily be read by such customers or suppliers, a notice containing the information required by this Chapter.
@ref s 1204(1) Disclosure required at business premises (src:16960-16964)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 1202 party` `s 1202 act`
`s 1204(1) the person must display the notice in the premises` MEANS
    PARTY `s 1202 the person to whom Chapter 2 applies`
    MUST `s 1204 display a notice containing the information required by Chapter 2 in a prominent position in the premises`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 1202 the person to whom Chapter 2 applies` BECAUSE "s 1204(1): no notice containing the information required by Chapter 2 was displayed in a prominent position in the premises"

§§ `Chapter 3: supplementary`

-- ---- s 1207: Application of general provisions about offences -------------------------------------------

-- src:16985 | 1207 Application of general provisions about offences
-- src:16986 | The provisions of sections 1121 to 1123 (liability of officer in default) and 1125 to 1131 (general provisions about offences) apply in relation to offences under this Part as in relation to offences under the Companies Acts.
@ref s 1207 Application of general provisions about offences (src:16985-16986)
GIVEN `the offence is an offence under Part 41` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of the section` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1207 the provision applies in relation to the offence` MEANS
    IF NOT `the offence is an offence under Part 41`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "apply in relation to offences under this Part"
    ELSE IF (`the number of the section` AT LEAST 1121 AND `the number of the section` AT MOST 1123)
            OR (`the number of the section` AT LEAST 1125 AND `the number of the section` AT MOST 1131)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): section 1207 names sections 1121 to 1123 and 1125 to 1131 and no other

-- ---- s 1208: Interpretation -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:16989 | “business” includes a profession;
@ref s 1208 "Business" (src:16989)
GIVEN `the activity is a profession` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1208 the activity is a business` MEANS
    IF `the activity is a profession`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“business” includes a profession"

-- src:16990 | “initial” includes any recognised abbreviation of a name;
@ref s 1208 "Initial" (src:16990)
GIVEN `the abbreviation is a recognised abbreviation of a name` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1208 the abbreviation is an initial` MEANS
    IF `the abbreviation is a recognised abbreviation of a name`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“initial” includes any recognised abbreviation of a name"

DECLARE `s 1208 kind of arrangement` IS ONE OF
    `s 1208 a partnership within the Partnership Act 1890`
    `s 1208 a limited partnership registered under the Limited Partnerships Act 1907`
    `s 1208 a firm or entity of a similar character formed under the law of a country or territory outside the United Kingdom`
    `s 1208 another arrangement`

-- src:16991 | “partnership” means—
-- src:16992 | (a) a partnership within the Partnership Act 1890 (c. 39), or
-- src:16993 | (b) a limited partnership registered under the Limited Partnerships Act 1907 (c. 24),
-- src:16994 | or a firm or entity of a similar character formed under the law of a country or territory outside the United Kingdom;
@ref s 1208 "Partnership" (src:16991-16994)
GIVEN arrangement IS A `s 1208 kind of arrangement`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1208 the arrangement is a partnership` MEANS
    CONSIDER arrangement
    WHEN `s 1208 another arrangement` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“partnership” means— (a) a partnership within the Partnership Act 1890 (c. 39), or (b) a limited partnership registered under the Limited Partnerships Act 1907 (c. 24), or a firm or entity of a similar character formed under the law of a country or territory outside the United Kingdom"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:16995 | “surname”, in relation to a peer or person usually known by a British title different from his surname, means the title by which he is known.
@ref s 1208 "Surname" (src:16995)
GIVEN `the person is a peer or a person usually known by a British title different from his surname` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the title by which he is known` IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 1208 the surname of the person` MEANS
    IF `the person is a peer or a person usually known by a British title different from his surname`
    THEN JUST `the title by which he is known`
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "“surname”, in relation to a peer or person usually known by a British title different from his surname"
